    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0017" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.01/167: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Boal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-03T22:00:00-04:00">January 3, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 4—1:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. La Paz papers today printed the full text of the Bolivian note of protest
                    delivered to Guani. The note, text and translation<anchor n="13" xml:id="d3-f1"
                    /> of which are being transmitted by pouch, states that the Committee in seeking
                    to consider matters such as the recognition of governments, exceeds its
                    authority and goes beyond the scope of activities for which it was originally
                    created. It insists that the matter of recognition is purely an individual
                    matter for each country to decide independently. The important thing in any
                    case, according to the note, is to win the war, and the delays occasioned by the
                    Montevideo discussions can only tend to limit Bolivia’s contribution temporarily
                    and therefore interfere with the war effort.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Boal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
